    "https://jobs.silkroad.com/ShenandoahUniversity/ShenandoahUniversity/jobs/3110": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Environmental Studies",
      "description": "Assistant Professor of Environmental Studies - 1460 University Drive, Winchester, Virginia, United States - Shenandoah University Skip Navigation Home Jobs My Account Menu Jobs My Account Loading... search chevron_left Shenandoah University Jobs Apply Assistant Professor of Environmental Studies ﻿ Job Location 1460 University Drive, Winchester, Virginia, United States Tracking Code 3110-306 The Department of Human and Environmental Health and Policy in the College of Arts and Sciences at Shenandoah University is seeking a dynamic and dedicated individual to join our faculty as an assistant professor in our environmental studies and conservation science and management programs (B.S. in Environmental Studies; B.S. in Conservation Science and Management; minor in Environmental Studies). Courses may include lectures, labs, and seminars that cover topics in environmental science and studies, forestry, wildlife management and geographic information systems (GIS). Shenandoah University, a private, comprehensive university located 70 miles northwest of Washington, D.C., is committed to increasing the diversity of the university community and the curriculum. Faculty members are expected to be active scholars in their fields and to participate in service to the university and the broader community. The Department of Human and Environmental Health and Policy has a student-centered focus that includes advising and mentoring, and fosters the academic success of an increasingly diverse student population. An on-campus, in-person presence is expected. Required Skills A doctoral degree in environmental science, studies, biology/ecology, or a closely related terminal degree by the start of the Fall 2026 semester. Demonstrates excellence in teaching, evidence of scholarly and professional activities, and experience teaching undergraduate courses. Required Experience The Environmental Studies Program at Shenandoah University seeks a dedicated, collegial faculty member to join our team. The ideal candidate will be passionate about environmental problems and solutions, committed to community engagement, student success, and ready to provide hands-on, immersive learning experiences for all students. We are particularly interested in candidates eager to collaborate across disciplines to develop upper-division courses and undergraduate learning and research opportunities in the broad fields of environmental science, studies, and wildlife management. Examples include, but are not limited to, wildlife conservation and management, human/wildlife interactions, geographic information systems (GIS), environmental/natural engineering, and waste management. We especially encourage bilingual candidates to apply. How to Apply: Complete application submissions will include a letter of intent, curriculum vitae, a research statement, a teaching statement, and contact information for three professional references. The review of applications will begin immediately and continue until a qualified candidate is selected. A pre-employment background check will be required. If the job requires driving for university business, a satisfactory driving record will also be required. **Note: A pre-employment background check will be required, and a satisfactory driving record may be required as a condition of hire. ** Authorization to work in the United States is a pre-condition of employment. At this time, Shenandoah University is not in a position to sponsor international visas. Shenandoah University values individuals and communities' unique and diverse perspectives locally and globally. It seeks to foster mutual understanding in an inviting community where individuals are welcome and respected. The university does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, ethnic or national origin, age, physical or mental disability, genetic information, veteran’s status, or on any other basis protected under applicable law. Salary Range $60,000.00 - $65,000.00 Salary Type Annually Apply Benefits and Policies Employee Benefits Drug & Alcohol Policy Shenandoah University Main page About Us Other Resources Sitemap close"
    },
    "https://jobs.silkroad.com/ShenandoahUniversity/ShenandoahUniversity/jobs/2831": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Management and Business Law",
      "description": "Assistant Professor of Management and Business Law - 1460 University Drive, Winchester, Virginia, United States - Shenandoah University Skip Navigation Home Jobs My Account Menu Jobs My Account Loading... search chevron_left Shenandoah University Jobs Apply Assistant Professor of Management and Business Law ﻿ Job Location 1460 University Drive, Winchester, Virginia, United States Tracking Code 2831-306 The School of Business at Shenandoah University invites applications for a full-time Assistant Professor of Management and Business Law beginning August 2026. This is a full-time benefited faculty appointment eligible for a multi-year career contract following a successful probationary period. This position is located on our main campus in Winchester, Virginia. We seek a dynamic educator-scholar who can contribute to both the Management and Legal/Ethics core of our AACSB-accredited undergraduate and graduate programs. The successful candidate will teach a versatile load that anchors the School’s compliance and human capital curriculum. Primary teaching responsibilities include Legal Environment of Business, Human Resource Management, and Business Ethics. In addition to undergraduate core courses, the successful candidate will contribute to the graduate level (MBA), specifically in areas such as Employment Law, Leadership, Human Resource Management, Business Ethics and/or Organizational Behavior. As a member of a small, collaborative faculty, the candidate will also be expected to support general business education (Intro to Business) and student mentorship. Strategic & Interdisciplinary Collaboration: The School is actively strengthening its focus on Ethical Leadership and Regulatory Compliance. The ideal candidate will demonstrate the ability to bridge the gap between legal theory and organizational practice. Healthcare Alignment: Experience or interest in Healthcare Law or Healthcare Management is a significant plus Corporate Governance: Candidates who can address emerging topics such as ESG (Environmental, Social, and Governance), AI Ethics, or Sustainability are especially encouraged to apply. Required Skills Required: Earned PhD or DBA in Management, Human Resources, Organizational Behavior, or related field. Candidates holding the Juris Doctor may be considered but are expected to have maintained a record of scholarship appropriate for this faculty appointment. ABD will be considered with completion prior to start date. Demonstrated ability to teach undergraduate courses in Business Law and Human Resources. Evidence of scholarly activity and/ or professional engagement consistent with AACSB \"Scholarly Academic\" (SA) status. Commitment to excellence in teaching and high-impact student engagement. Preferred: Interest or expertise in Healthcare Law/Policy or Healthcare Systems. Experience teaching at the Graduate (MBA) level. Professional certifications in HR (e.g., SHRM-CP/SCP) or related management fields. Industry experience in corporate compliance, labor relations, or executive leadership. The Shenandoah University School of Business is AACSB-accredited and prepares students to lead and manage complex organizations in a dynamic global economy. The School emphasizes innovation, ethical leadership, experiential learning, and strong connections to industry and community partners. How to Apply: The complete application will include a cover letter, resume, and contact information for three professional references. Inquiries for the Position Should Be Addressed to: Dr. Michael Magro, Associate Dean, School of Business, mmagro@su.edu. Application Deadline Date: March 20, but applications will be considered as soon as they are received. Applications received after this date may be considered until the position is filled. **Note: A pre-employment background check will be required, and a satisfactory driving record may be required as a condition of hire. **Authorized to work in the United States is a pre-condition of employment. At this time, Shenandoah University is not in a position to sponsor international visas. Shenandoah University values individuals and communities' unique and diverse perspectives locally and globally. It seeks to foster mutual understanding in an inviting community where individuals are welcome and respected. The university does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, physical or mental disability, genetic information, veteran’s status, or on any other basis protected under applicable law. Salary Range $75,000.00 - $85,000.00 Salary Type Not Applicable Apply Benefits and Policies Employee Benefits Drug & Alcohol Policy Shenandoah University Main page About Us Other Resources Sitemap close"
    },
    "https://jobs.silkroad.com/ShenandoahUniversity/ShenandoahUniversity/jobs/3111": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Dance",
      "description": "Assistant Professor, Dance - Musical Theatre & Jazz Focus, Shenandoah Conservatory  - 1460 University Drive, Winchester, Virginia, United States - Shenandoah University Skip Navigation Home Jobs My Account Menu Jobs My Account Loading... search chevron_left Shenandoah University Jobs Apply Assistant Professor, Dance - Musical Theatre & Jazz Focus, Shenandoah Conservatory ﻿ Job Location 1460 University Drive, Winchester, Virginia, United States Tracking Code 3111-306 Shenandoah University’s Dance Department is accepting applications for an Assistant Professor of Dance (Musical Theatre & Jazz Focus) in the Shenandoah Conservatory. This is a full-time benefited position located on our main campus in Winchester, Virginia. Shenandoah Conservatory of Shenandoah University seeks an exceptional teacher, with a focus on Musical Theatre and Jazz Dance, to join its dynamic performing arts faculty. This full time and career-contract track Assistant Professor position will begin in August of 2027. The Dance Department & The Musical Theatre Program: The Dance Department engages close to 60 dance majors and 100 musical theatre students in rigorous professional training that is equally grounded in ballet, modern dance, and jazz training. Core training is complemented by an extensive composition sequence, three mainstage concerts per year in the 600-seat Ohrstrom-Bryant Theatre, and numerous opportunities for creative & performance work. Extensive outreach opportunities include international performance-and-study tours. The Dance Ensemble has been featured in concerts at the Kennedy Center, Strathmore Hall, and other professional venues in New York City, Philadelphia, Baltimore and Washington, DC. Shenandoah Conservatory's BFA Musical Theatre degree is among most selective and the longestestablished programs in the country. With a continuing reputation for excellence in pre-professional training and a constant eye on the industry, the program provides highly individualized education in a rigorous, yet supportive environment. The school's geography allows for easy access to and regular interaction with theatre professionals from New York City as well as Washington D.C. Grounded in the foundations of musical theatre, the program places primary emphasis on contemporary trends and current musical styles, including pop/rock musicals and vocal technique, entrepreneurship, and digital media. About the Shenandoah Conservatory and University: Shenandoah Conservatory was founded in 1875 and is located at the head of the historic Shenandoah Valley in Winchester, VA, 70 miles west of Washington, DC. Over 650 students are enrolled in baccalaureate, master's, and doctoral curricula in the areas of music, theater, and dance, and are taught by a dynamic and diverse faculty of over 125, half of whom are full-time. Shenandoah University is a diverse institution of approximately 4,000 students enrolled in baccalaureate, masters and doctoral curricula in business, arts and sciences, health professions and performing arts. Shenandoah University is an independent, coeducational institution affiliated with the United Methodist Church and is accredited by the Southern Association of Colleges and Schools. www.su.edu. Shenandoah University is committed to enriching its educational experience and culture through the diversity of its faculty, administration, and staff. All candidates are strongly encouraged to include a statement in their cover letters addressing ways in which they may be able to contribute to that commitment. Responsibilities : The successful candidate will serve as a member of the Dance Department faculty and collaborate closely with both the Dance and Musical Theatre programs in fulfilling the following responsibilities: teach musical theatre dance styles and jazz techniques for dance majors, musical theatre majors, and non-majors; teach additional movement-based courses per expertise, as needed; contribute choreography and movement direction for Dance Department and Musical Theatre productions; and actively participate in Departmental, Conservatory, and University activities, including advising, recruitment, auditions, mentorship, and committee service. Additional teaching assignments for the position will be based on areas of expertise/interest. Required Skills Requirements : Candidates will be expected to possess the following: A national profile in dance performance with significant experience related to musical theatre productions; A significant portfolio of creative/scholarly work in choreography and/or publication; A terminal degree in Musical Theatre or Dance; A record of successful teaching at the collegiate level; and, A demonstrated ability to thrive within an intensive but collegial Conservatory environment. Choreographic experience in a variety of settings (musical theatre productions, classical jazz, industry settings, etc.) is highly desirable. Required Experience How to Apply: Complete application submissions will include a letter of intent, curriculum vitae, and contact information for three professional references. The review of applications will begin immediately and continue until a qualified candidate is selected. A pre-employment background check will be required. If the job requires driving for University business, a satisfactory driving record will also be required. **Note: A pre-employment background check will be required, and a satisfactory driving record may be required as a condition of hire. ** Authorization to work in the United States is a pre-condition of employment. At this time, Shenandoah University is not in a position to sponsor international visas. Shenandoah University values individuals and communities' unique and diverse perspectives locally and globally. It seeks to foster mutual understanding in an inviting community where individuals are welcome and respected. The university does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, ethnic or national origin, age, physical or mental disability, genetic information, veteran’s status, or on any other basis protected under applicable law. Salary Range $65,000.00 - $70,000.00 Salary Type Annually Apply Benefits and Policies Employee Benefits Drug & Alcohol Policy Shenandoah University Main page About Us Other Resources Sitemap close"
    },
    "https://jobs.silkroad.com/ShenandoahUniversity/ShenandoahUniversity/jobs/2424": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor of Pharmacy Practice",
      "description": "Assistant/Associate Professor of Pharmacy Practice - 1775 N Sector Ct, Winchester, Virginia, United States - Shenandoah University Skip Navigation Home Jobs My Account Menu Jobs My Account Loading... search chevron_left Shenandoah University Jobs Apply Assistant/Associate Professor of Pharmacy Practice ﻿ Job Location 1775 N Sector Ct, Winchester, Virginia, United States Tracking Code 2424-306 Shenandoah University’s School of Pharmacy is accepting applications for an Assistant/Associate Professor of Pharmacy Practice position. This is a full-time, benefited position located on our Health Professions campus in Winchester, Virginia. This position emphasizes pharmacy practice and patient care in an ambulatory or acute care setting in Winchester, VA. The primary clinical responsibilities of the faculty member will be the provision of patient care encompassing a broad range of disease states with an emphasis on acute/chronic diseases and medication management. They may be involved in implementing other patient care services. The faculty member will also serve as a preceptor for IPPE and APPE students. Didactic teaching will primarily occur within the School of Pharmacy’s therapeutic modules, patient assessment skills, or case-based laboratory courses. Service and scholarship responsibilities will be determined by faculty rank. Required Skills The candidate should possess an in-depth understanding of clinical ambulatory care/acute care pharmacy practice, strong interpersonal and organizational skills, and the ability to develop and work within innovative pharmacy practice models. A pharmacy practice (PGY1) residency or the ability to demonstrate equivalent experience in pharmacy practice is required. Candidates with prior academic experience or additional training (PGY2 or fellowship) are encouraged to apply. Required Experience The candidate should possess a Pharm.D. degree and be eligible for pharmacy licensure in the State of Virginia. How to Apply: The complete application will include a letter of intent, curriculum vitae, and contact information for three professional references. Applications will be reviewed immediately and continue until a qualified candidate is selected. Shenandoah University is committed to enriching its educational experience and culture through the diversity of its faculty, administration, and staff. All candidates are strongly encouraged to include a statement in their cover letters addressing ways in which they can contribute to that commitment. **Note: A pre-employment background check will be required, and a satisfactory driving record may be required as a condition of hire. Authorized to work in the United States is a pre-condition of employment. At this time, Shenandoah University is not in a position to sponsor international visas. Shenandoah University values the unique and diverse perspectives of individuals and communities locally and globally and seeks to foster mutual understanding in an inviting community where individuals are welcome and respected. The university does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, physical or mental disability, genetic information, veteran’s status, or on any other basis protected under applicable law. Salary Range $110,000.00 - $120,000.00 Salary Type Annually Apply Benefits and Policies Employee Benefits Drug & Alcohol Policy Shenandoah University Main page About Us Other Resources Sitemap close"
